                                // `uval == 0` arm.  Same behaviour, different
                                // mechanism; a future pass that widens this to
                                // a caller which DOES consult `invalidValue`
                                // must not carry the old sentence over.  That
                                // is why the old `!fb9.isUnknown()` guard goes.
